<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62617" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λευκαία</span></b> , ἡ, a synonym
		(perh. a variety) of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπάρτος</span>, used for
		cordage or tackle, <i><span class="en">
			Moschio
		</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
			Ath.
			5.206f
		</span></i>:—written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λευκέα</span></b>  in <i><span class="en">
			<u>BGU</u>
			544.5
		</span></i>
		<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Artem.
			3.59
		</span></i> (who dists. it from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάνναβις</span>), <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεύκη</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11.1
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λευκαίας στέφανος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(1).155
				</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				 iii 79
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				 iv 118
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λευκαῖος</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεύς</span>, Zeus <i>of the white
			poplar</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				5.5.5
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
